    "body": "## Description\n\nUpgrade AWEX from 0.8.2 to 0.9.0 in both the SGLang and vLLM manifests and regenerate both lockfiles, following the scope of #1621. No other package versions change. AWEX 0.9.0 declares `cloudpickle>=2.2`; the existing locked version already satisfies this requirement.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nN/A. Reference: #1621.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\nDependency maintenance; the template has no dependency-specific type.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [ ] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [x] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):**\n\nNo incompatibility identified by the static checks below. GPU runtime compatibility remains unverified.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nValidation:\n\n- `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=https://pypi.org/simple bash scripts/uv_lock.sh`\n- `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=https://pypi.org/simple pre-commit run --all-files` (passed in an isolated clone with the repository virtualenv)\n- `git diff --check`\n- Parsed both lockfiles and confirmed that AWEX is the only package whose version changed.\n- Compared the 0.8.2 and 0.9.0 wheel sources across 22 imported AWEX modules; no missing modules or signature changes found among directly referenced definitions. Verified downloaded wheel hashes against PyPI metadata.\n\nGPU/NCCL multi-process weight-transfer integration tests were not run because the local macOS environment lacks CUDA hardware. This static validation does not establish distributed runtime correctness.\n",
